WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:04.173
The Dormouse came and sat next to Alice.

2
00:00:04.193 --> 00:00:09.534
As Alice began to grow, she thought she should leave the courtroom.

3
00:00:09.554 --> 00:00:16.756
But she was curious about the trial.

4
00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:32.890
So she decided to stay for as long as there was room for her.

5
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:40.535
"I wish you wouldn't squeeze me like that," the Dormouse complained to Alice.

6
00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:44.617
"I can hardly breathe," the Gryphon said.

7
00:00:44.637 --> 00:00:47.299
"I can't help it," Alice said.

8
00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:48.839
"I'm growing."

9
00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:55.083
"Well, you have no right to grow here!"

10
00:00:55.403 --> 00:00:56.364
the Dormouse said.

11
00:00:57.608 --> 00:00:59.869
His comment annoyed Alice.

12
00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:01.769
"Don't talk nonsense.

13
00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:04.930
You know that you're growing too," she said.

14
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:10.031
"Yes, but he doesn't do it all at once," the Gryphon said.

15
00:01:11.432 --> 00:01:15.133
The Dormouse and he got up and sat on the other side of the courtroom.

16
00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.595
Meanwhile the Queen kept staring at the Hatter.

17
00:01:24.535 --> 00:01:26.436
She waved to one of the soldiers.

18
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.584
"Bring me the list of the singers in the last concert," she said.

19
00:01:33.344 --> 00:01:36.987
When the Hatter heard this, he started to shake again.

20
00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:43.671
"Tell us your story right now," the King said angrily.

21
00:01:43.691 --> 00:01:47.394
"Or I'll have you put to death."

22
00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:52.898
"I'm a poor man, Your Majesty."

23
00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:55.240
The Hatter spoke in a shaky voice.

24
00:01:56.296 --> 00:01:58.317
"I'd just sat down for tea.

25
00:01:58.477 --> 00:02:05.580
And then there was the twinkling of tea and—" "The twinkling of what?"

26
00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.061
the King asked.

27
00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:11.382
"It began with the tea," the Hatter replied.

28
00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:18.265
"Of course, the word twinkling begins with a T.

29
00:02:18.965 --> 00:02:20.526
I'm not stupid!"

30
00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:24.908
The King was growing more impatient every moment.

31
00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:27.929
"Go on with your story."

32
00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:36.791
"After the tea twinkled, the March Hare said—" "I didn't!"

33
00:02:37.191 --> 00:02:38.512
the March Hare interrupted.

34
00:02:38.532 --> 00:02:39.972
"You did!"

35
00:02:40.212 --> 00:02:41.312
the Hatter insisted.

36
00:02:41.332 --> 00:02:43.353
"I deny it!"

37
00:02:43.713 --> 00:02:44.853
the March Hare said.

38
00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:49.055
"He denies it," the King said to the Hatter.

39
00:02:49.075 --> 00:02:53.736
"Leave out the March Hare and continue your story."

40
00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.549
Alice looked at the jury box.

41
00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:04.092
All the jurors crossed out "I deny it" on their slates.

42
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:15.638
"Those two guinea pigs have made a real mess of their slates," she thought.

43
00:03:15.658 --> 00:03:25.024
"Well, then the Dormouse said The Hatter looked anxiously at the Dormouse, expecting him to deny everything too.

44
00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.021
But the Dormouse was fast asleep.

45
00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:34.104
"After that," the Hatter said, "I had more bread and butter."

46
00:03:34.124 --> 00:03:37.085
"But what did the Dormouse say?"

47
00:03:37.545 --> 00:03:40.666
one guinea pig asked.

48
00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:42.987
"I really can't remember," the Hatter said.

49
00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:49.910
"You must remember, or you'll be put to death," the King said.

50
00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.492
The Hatter dropped his teacup and his bread and butter.

51
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.082
He went down on one knee in front of the King.

52
00:03:57.102 --> 00:04:01.866
"I'm a poor man, Your Majesty," he repeated.

53
00:04:01.886 --> 00:04:07.731
"You're a very poor speaker," the King said.

54
00:04:07.751 --> 00:04:12.935
"Woo-hoo!" Here the second guinea pig cheered.

55
00:04:13.936 --> 00:04:16.258
A soldier immediately took it away.

56
00:04:16.278 --> 00:04:23.304
"If that's all you know, you may leave," the King said to the Hatter.

57
00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:29.906
And here the other guinea pig cheered and was removed from the jury box.

58
00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:36.169
"I'd rather finish my tea first," the Hatter said.

59
00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:41.431
He shot a quick look at the Queen, who was reading the list of singers.

60
00:04:42.832 --> 00:04:45.573
"You may go," the King said.

61
00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.754
The Hatter rushed from the courtroom.

62
00:04:48.774 --> 00:04:55.542
"Just take his head off outside," the Queen said to one of the soldiers.

63
00:04:58.024 --> 00:05:02.067
But the Hatter was out of sight before the soldier got to the doors.

64
00:05:03.688 --> 00:05:05.750
Alice shook her head in disbelief.

65
00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.452
"The Hatter wasn't any help at all.

66
00:05:09.253 --> 00:05:13.456
At this rate, we'll never find out if the Knave of Hearts is guilty," she thought.

67
00:05:13.476 --> 00:05:16.839
"Call the next witness!"

68
00:05:17.279 --> 00:05:17.980
the King said.
